    "focus": "Cancer stem cells, patient-derived organoids and neurogenesis",
    "bio": "Wassim Abou-Kheir founded the WAKers at the American University of Beirut in 2011. He studied at the Lebanese University and AUB, completed his PhD fellowship at the Albert Einstein College of Medicine, and trained as a postdoctoral fellow at the National Cancer Institute (NIH), where he studied stem/progenitor cells in prostate cancer models.\n\nAt AUB he teaches and coordinates courses for undergraduate, graduate and medical students, and has mentored more than 200 students and early-career researchers. He is active in the AACR, ISSCR, SfN and EACR, and was a TWAS Young Affiliate (2013–2017).",
